# Workflow plan step W4 (docs/WORKFLOW_PLAN.md, 2026-11-14): one home per setting. A case Physics > Setup owns (the duct example,
# from the STL mesher) shows its solver and run length on the Run page as a read-out from Setup (with a Change button and
# "Edit here" for the fields); Numerics offers Setup's preset (Robust / Balanced / Accurate) itself, the schemes behind Every scheme.
shell $QC_TESTS/../build/test_stlmesh example duct $SB/ws/w4-duct > $OUT/example.log 2>&1
open $SB/ws/w4-duct
wait 10
click nav:physics
wait 10
click su-write
wait 30
click nav:run
wait-until page Run
wait 10
assert text From Physics > Setup
assert widget run-change
assert not widget dict:system/controlDict:endTime
screenshot $OUT/w4_run.png
click run-edit-here
wait 5
assert text End time
click nav:numerics
wait-until page Numerics
wait 10
assert text Numerics preset
assert widget num-preset#1
assert not widget num-tabs#0
click num-preset#0
wait 10
assert text First-order upwind
shell grep -q 'numerics = robust' $SB/ws/w4-duct/simulation.ini && touch $OUT/robust
assert file $OUT/robust
assert text Setup changed: write again
click num-every
wait 5
assert widget num-tabs#0
screenshot $OUT/w4_numerics.png
